{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_13-51-31-omnipaxos-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd={\n \\\"rationale\\\": (\\\"The generalized probe executed green and confirms the accept-phase gap at three nodes, so the 'only the 2-node configuration was probed' limit is replaced by a measurement spanning both sizes; one operand of the new case (extra Accepted traffic) is recorded as an open observation rather than explained away.\\\"),\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"1a5428f0aa284eb1a2a3f1a083fcb052-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"224b9ea47a35472db872f526b5cf4392-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"src_leader_resend\\\",\\\"src_follower_resend\\\",\\\"src_follower_flush_batch\\\",\\\"src_follower_acceptsync_reply\\\",\\\"src_leader_handle_accepted\\\",\\\"src_resend_dispatch\\\",\\\"src_outgoing_trim_doc\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"9f3f25cc1783466ab2a5b0b6be9aa7d7\\\":[3,1,0,4,2]},\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"holds\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\": (\\\"Current account. Source: the accept phase has no self-initiated refresh of the leader's knowledge of a follower's acceptance - resend_messages_leader's Accept arm only re-Prepares peers that are not promised and resends a pending StopSign or its decide (leader.rs:371-403), resend_messages_follower's Accept arm is empty \\\"\n   \\\"(follower.rs:240-269), and flush_batch_follower replies only when the flush itself advanced the accepted index (follower.rs:284-290) - while the leader decides from advertised accepted indexes (leader.rs:316-345). Retained execution 9f3f25cc1783466ab2a5b0b6be9aa7d7 (experiment 224b9ea47a35472db872f526b5cf4392-experiment, exit 0, three cases passed, \\\"\n   \\\"parsing_error_count 0) measures the gap at both cluster sizes in one run. Three nodes, event 3 \"'`three_node_lost_accepteds_window`: steps 500, resend_periods 100, produced BLE:2025, Prepare:2, Promise:2, AcceptSync:2, Accepted:4, AcceptDecide:2, dropped 2 Accepted receipts, accept_decide_total 2 (the single proposal'\"'s one AcceptDecide per promised follower, so no new proposal was made), \\\"\n   \\\"leader_decided_idx 0, follower_2_accepted_idx 1, follower_3_accepted_idx 1, both_followers_hold_undecided_entry true - i.e. with both receipts that the write quorum still needed removed, the leader stayed at decided 0 for 100 configured resend periods while both followers really held the entry, and event 4 \"'`three_node_later_proposal_repairs` shows the later unrelated proposal deciding both entries in 1 step \"\n   \"(leader_decided_idx 2). Two nodes, the same run: event 1 `lost_accepted_window` (dropped Accepted:1, accept_decide_total 1, after_drop BLE:667 only, leader_decided_idx 0, follower_accepted_idx 1, follower_holds_undecided_entry true, leader_still_stable true) with the delivered control event 0 `delivered_accepted_decides` deciding in 1 step and event 2 `later_proposal_repairs` repairing in 1 step. The comparison therefore holds at both sizes: the entry stays \"\n   \"undecided for at least 100 resend periods whenever the lost receipts are exactly those the write quorum still needs, with no protocol traffic beyond heartbeats in the two-node case, and progress requires a later proposal (or a ballot change, which changes the case). Scope and fault assumption: one lost receipt in a two-node cluster, or two lost receipts in a three-node cluster - i.e. the losses must remove the quorum'\"'s completion, which is a bounded and stated assumption, not an arbitrary \\\"\n   \\\"message-loss rate. Counter-limitations kept in force: (a) clusters are two and three nodes only, and the loss pattern is chosen to be quorum-critical; (b) a client-side retry can repair the earlier entry as a side effect, so the practical impact depends on the caller's retry policy - the probe deliberately makes no further proposal; (c) one observation is not explained: the three-node case produced four Accepted messages and \"'`after_drop` still shows one Accepted crossing the wire, yet the leader did not decide; either those messages did not carry the entry'\"'s accepted index to the leader or another mechanism suppressed the decision, and this is recorded as an open question about the \\\"\n   \\\"probe's message accounting rather than as target behaviour; (d) a new Prepare/Promise cycle re-advertises acceptance through handle_acceptsync's reply (follower.rs:53-79), which is why the earlier cadence-confounded run appeared repaired - this probe holds leadership stable to keep that path out of the window.\\\"),\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"Only two- and three-node clusters are probed, with the loss pattern chosen so that the losses are exactly what the write quorum still needs.\\\",\n   \\\"Client-side retry can repair the earlier entry as a side effect; the probe deliberately makes no further proposal.\\\",\n   \\\"Unexplained observation: the three-node case's message accounting shows Accepted:4 produced and an Accepted crossing after the drop while the leader still did not decide; the probe's accounting of who sent what is not yet explained.\\\",\n   \\\"The repair that a ballot change provides (re-advertising through handle_acceptsync) is deliberately excluded by keeping leadership stable during the window.\\\"]\n }]\n}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
